# Form Input Font

Apply to every **text-like form control** in the web UI (`apps/web`): create/edit forms, dialogs, drawers, settings, auth, search filters, and generate steps.

## Rules

1. **Add `font-mono`** — Every `<input>` and `<textarea>` that accepts user-typed text must include the Tailwind `font-mono` class on the element (or on a shared input className constant that includes it).

2. **Text-like inputs** — Applies to `type="text"`, `type="search"`, `type="email"`, `type="password"`, `type="number"`, `type="date"`, `type="url"`, `type="tel"`, and `<textarea>`. Also applies when `type` is omitted and the control behaves as a text field.

3. **Exceptions** — Do **not** add `font-mono` to checkbox, radio, range, file, hidden, submit, or button inputs. Labels, buttons, and read-only display text follow their own typography rules unless they are the input itself.

4. **Shared classNames** — When extracting a reusable input class string, include `font-mono` in that shared value so new fields inherit the rule automatically.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — sans-serif on a text field
<input
  value={name}
  onChange={...}
  className="w-full rounded-md border border-border bg-background px-3 py-2 outline-none focus:border-muted"
/>

// ✅ GOOD
<textarea
  value={facts}
  onChange={...}
  className="w-full rounded-md border border-border bg-background px-3 py-2 font-mono text-sm outline-none focus:border-muted"
/>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — checkbox styled as form control
<input type="checkbox" className="font-mono h-4 w-4" />

// ✅ GOOD — checkbox keeps default sizing only
<input type="checkbox" className="h-4 w-4 rounded border-border" />
```
